  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "an opening orifice installed in the solenoid operated valve, out-of-specification clearance tolerance between the valve plug and valve cage, and a two-phase/choked-flow condition due to the closed block valve combined to cause the pressurizer PORV to fail to open; root causes were a maintenance procedure lacking guidance to verify orifice removal and validate plug/cage clearances, and inadequate implementation of a design change package that introduced an SOV with an opening orifice, resulting in loss of configuration management",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "procedure/configuration-management weakness leading to PORV mechanical failure",
    "provisional": true
  },
